Fix clock race in TOTP previous windows tests

test_with_passcode_in_previous_windows_default and _extended
(keystone/tests/unit/test_v3_auth.py) derive the time of the passcode
from the current time and then stop the clock with TimeFixture(),
which reads the current time again. The TOTP auth plugin
(keystone/auth/plugins/totp.py) accepts the window of the stopped clock
and the included_previous_windows windows before it. If a 30 second
TOTP window boundary passes between the two reads, the passcode is one
window older than the test intends, and the plugin answers 401.
test_with_passcode_no_previous_windows generates its passcode before it
stops the clock and has the same race. test-service-images (keystone,
2026.1) failed this way in
test_with_passcode_in_previous_windows_default on PR #1546 (run
40139432029): "Bad response: 401 UNAUTHORIZED (not 201)".

The two previous windows tests now read the current time once and stop
the clock at it, so the window of the passcode and the windows the
plugin accepts derive from the same instant.
test_with_passcode_no_previous_windows stops the clock before it
generates the passcode, as the other TOTP tests do. The assertions are
unchanged. With the wall clock forced past a window boundary between
the two reads, all three tests fail on 29.0.0 with that 401 and pass
with the patch.

The patch changes test code only, so it changes nothing at runtime and
tests/container-images/verify_keystone.sh needs no assertion. It leaves
out the release note of the upstream change. Its 2026.2 twin,
patches/keystone/2026.2/0002-fix-clock-race-in-totp-previous-windows-tests.patch,
carries the same hunks, cut from 30.0.0.

Applies to keystone 29.0.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: proposed as
https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/keystone/+/1012064.

